t=\"_blank\"><b>Spirited Away.</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Fetched my DVD and watching now. Miyazaki does good stuff. Also thinking about My Neighbor Totoro for some of the wonderful side of the fae world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T19:51:46-08:00","id":1031936,"title":"","content":"One movie I'm surprised hasn't been mentioned is Changeling, while the 2nd half of the movie isn't exactly relevant to Changeling the Lost, the first half is very unsettling to look at if you watch it with it the game in mind. It's from the point of view of a mother who believes her child has been abducted and replaced by another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6314-scynths","name":"scynths","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T17:01:46-07:00","id":1139301,"title":"","content":"Kubo and the Two Strings, Rise of the Guardians. Watch these two with the idea that The Man in the Moon as a true fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T17:27:36-07:00","id":1141595,"title":"","content":"City of Lost Children works for me. \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:52:46-07:00","id":1142218,"title":"","content":"One of my favorites is <i>MirrorMask</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:35:46-07:00","id":1142240,"title":"","content":"One of those I look at at and has not been mentioned already is Don't Be Afraid Of The Dark","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:33:52-07:00","id":1142263,"title":"","content":"I recommend &quot;The Never Ending Story, Legend, Stardust, also Try Ink. ( Though that's more of a Changeling/Mage Crossover movie)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:49:54-07:00","id":1142272,"title":"","content":"Pirates of the Caribbean 2 - Folks are shanghai'd by a creepy otherworldly pirate ship and its cthonic captain. Sailors slowly find themselves transforming into fantastical marine hybrids. sounds pretty changeling to me. (minus the whole psychopomp angle)<br /> <br /> Peter Pan (2003 version) - I have always thought that Peter Pan was a particularly great changeling story and the 2003 adaptation has the dark undertones that make it particularly suitable for Lost. My spin on it is that Tinkerbell is the Keeper and Peter Pan is her loyalist, who goes into forays into the Waking World to abduct children to bring into her Arcadian Realm to play out her crazy fantasies.<br /> <br /> Thale - A scandinavian film about crime scene cleaners who find a strange fairy creature that has been the subject of horrible experiments. The enigmatic cow tailed &quot;hulder&quot; girl is a pretty good model for a freshly escaped changeling.<br /> <br /> Mars Needs Moms - Aliens kidnap the protagonists mother in order to extract her essence to power their caretaker robots ... it is a kid's movie, obviously, but pretty creepy and we all know about the connection between alien abductions and changeling mythology.<br /> <br /> (Not a movie, but relevant)<br /> <br /> Samurai Jack - A great hero battles against a powerful, phantasmagorical incarnation of evil and gets flung into the far distant &quot;future&quot; filled with strange creatures, robots and monsters all powered by the essence of said incarnate evil ... lots of changeling themes here.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 09-20-2017, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T06:39:44-07:00","id":1146318,"title":"","content":"Im severely disappointed no ones made mention of Coraline. Considering it seems to point for point feel like a Changeling game with the focus beinh arcadia and the eventual escaping with as much you intact as possible","signature":"","edited"