e and the holiday season... The Santa Clause. It is definitely a Wyrd enforced legal pledge that Scott Calvin accidentally stumbled into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this make Scott Calvin from that film series a Goblin Queen? If so...AWESOME!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T23:44:41-08:00","id":1164978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1027308-ctl-movies?p=1164817#post1164817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally not my first thought, but also totally appropriate for both the game and the holiday season... The Santa Clause. It is definitely a Wyrd enforced legal pledge that Scott Calvin accidentally stumbled into.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me most <b>CtL</b> holiday season movie is...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3850590/\" target=\"_blank\"><i><b>Krampus </b></i>( 2015 with Adam Scott )</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9k-uig5obaA\" data-code=\"9k-uig5obaA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9k-uig5obaA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's basiclly story of True Fae looking as 'German bad Santa Clause' taking vangence on whole family, ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( I need to rewatch it with my partner this year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:38:27-08:00","id":1165287,"title":"","content":"Bit of an odd choice, but Grosse Point Blank. We've got a guy who joined the military before he even graduates, and then was &quot;taken&quot; to be trained and made into a professional killer. He &quot;gets out&quot; and keeps doing what he knows from those days, but it doesn't make him happy (or well-adjusted). At some point he realizes he hates what he has become and tries to turn over a new leaf. But a guy/group tries to pull him back into that life against his will, even threatening his agency/life if he doesn't just become one of them. If you replace &quot;assassin&quot; with loyalist, the story takes on a particular vibe. Even him going home and finding it's gone fits. Now I feel I've gotta watch that again to see how well it holds up under my theory watching it<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, maybe he only escaped around the beginning of the movie. So he's not a loyalist ever, but they're still trying to make him one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 12-05-2017, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:01:51-08:00","id":1167316,"title":"","content":"The new edition mentions the Marvel/Netflix series Jessica Jones as a potential source of inspiration, but many of the Marvel Cinematic heroes could serve as inspiration for Changeling characters, having gone through a similar process of being taken, transformed, and then released into a world that is not built for them: Captain America, Iron Man, Black Widow, Winter Soldier, Luke Cage, Iron Fist, Starlord, Gamora and Nebula all have had some part of the Changeling experience.<br /> <br /> A few of the antagonists also could serve as inspiration for Gentry NPCs: Loki, Odin, Hela and the Grandmaster from the Thor films; Thanos (especially in Guardians of the Galaxy); Ego; Dormammu; even Ultron and Daredevil's Kingpin are interesting, if not perfect, models the True Fae.<br /> <br /> And that's not even touching on the rich vein of the original comic sources...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T19:16:07-07:00","id":1247869,"title":"","content":"Ancient aliens on the History channel. They've had episodes on the gods, superheroes, conflicts between opposing factions (the Seelie and Unseelie courts), aliens underground (the Fir Bolg), aliens underwater (the Fomoire). They haven't had an episode on cities in the sky (the Tuatha de Danann) but they have frequently referenced it in other episodes. They've had several episodes on the taken and the returned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T15:20:52-07:00","id":1250082,"title":"","content":"I'm going back to the classics.<br /> <br /> Beauty and the Beast. Especially the new live action movie.<br /> Watch it with the idea that the old hag (whom the prince mistreats) is a True Fae who pulls the entire castle grounds into the Hedge. Maurice found his way there when he got lost in a storm, but when he returned with Gaston and Lefou, the way was no longer there. It's always winter inside the grounds and those imprisoned there get fae miens and powers to fit them.<br /> <br /> Pinocchio. The 1940 Disney version. This movie is SO DARK. Pinocchio himself is a fetch who got his shadow from the blue fairy. Pleasure Island, the carnival town that Pinocchio and the boys are taken to is in Arcadia. There, he and the boys get turned into donkeys (kind of a fae mien) to be sold for slave labor, before he escapes half-turned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T15:36:24-07:00","id":1250087,"title":"","content":"I can recommend two more titles:<br /> <br /> &quot;Song of the Sea&quot; is full of fae creatures and seems to be inspired both by Irish and Norse mythology. It's a sweet and wonderful piece of animated film.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell&quot;, a series based upon the book with the same name - and done very well. (I actually prefer the series over the book.)<br /> A mage during the Napoleon era wants to brings back magic to England. In a show of authenticity, he promises to revive the wife of a lord... and does so by lending power from a fairy. All the fairy asks for in return is for her to be his for half of her remaining life...<br /> You get to see the roads of the Hedge with Arcadia waiting on the other side, the cunning nature of the Fae and some pretty cool-ass shows of magic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}